      "body": "## Purpose\n\nFixes #60971. `--enable-log-outputs` (and `--enable-log-deltas`) were accepted as server-wide flags but never forwarded to the Anthropic `/v1/messages` handler, so output logging stayed at its parent defaults there even though `create_messages` reuses the shared `create_chat_completion` implementation where the logging is gated on `self.enable_log_outputs`.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n- `AnthropicServingMessages.__init__` now accepts `enable_log_outputs` / `enable_log_deltas` (defaults matching the parent: `False` / `True`) and forwards both to `OpenAIServingChat.__init__`.\n- `init_generate_state` passes `args.enable_log_outputs` / `args.enable_log_deltas` when constructing the handler, same as the adjacent Chat Completions setup.\n\n## Why this is not duplicating existing work\n\nThe issue (filed today) has no linked PR. Searched open PRs for `60971` and for `enable_log_outputs anthropic`; nothing open or merged touches the Anthropic handler's flag wiring.\n\n## Test plan\n\nTests removed per maintainer review; the change is constructor-level flag forwarding only, covered by CI.\n\n## AI assistance disclosure\n\nPrepared with AI assistance (Kimi K3). The submitter reviewed every changed line and ran the tests above.\n\n",
